{"title":"Number line","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Number_line&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p><p>A <b>number line</b> is a pictoral representation of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a>; it is typically represented as a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">line</a> with tick marks, where each tick mark represents an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a>.  Often, the number line has the the integer <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Zero\" title=\"Zero\">zero</a> in the middle, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> numbers to the right and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Negative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Negative\">negative</a> numbers to the left. Conceptually, the number line continues indefinitely. Often a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> axis is used to represent <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_number\" title=\"Imaginary number\">imaginary numbers</a>, which is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_plane\" title=\"Complex plane\">complex plane</a>.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Images.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b7/Images.jpg/300px-Images.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"104\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/b7/Images.jpg 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption>A number line.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_plane\" title=\"Complex plane\">Complex plane</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_number\" title=\"Complex number\">Complex number</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234218\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 20/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.335      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.335      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5083:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234218 and revision id 42756. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}